From c417cc8a9afc97e5702f97a26c0063418f26a399 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:58:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers of Trilinos: fifth review

- the rows of the converted matrices are sorted by
  KokkosSparse::sort_crs_matrix (the insertion sort was slow on the long
  rows of high order elements, on the host); the conversion on the GPU
  takes 0.023 seconds instead of 0.064 on the beam of 421,443 unknowns;
- MueLu: the products of sparse matrices of Kokkos Kernels (SPGEMM_KK)
  are only selected when each GPU of the node serves one process: Kokkos
  Kernels reserves up to half the free memory of the GPU for each product,
  and three processes sharing a GPU ran out of memory (randomly);
- CMake: when the paths of the configurations of Kokkos differ, the
  versions (KokkosConfigVersion.cmake) and the configurations
  (KokkosCore_config.h) are compared (KokkosConfig.cmake is the same for
  all the installations);
- Amesos2: all the names of Tacho use the default node;
- an operator whose setup failed throws when applied;
- hybrid GMRES without outer solver: a maximum number of iterations is
  refused, as a tolerance;
- the hypre arrays read on the GPU are synchronized before the
  conversion;
- test of the reuse of the whole hierarchy compared to the reuse of the
  prolongators, with a margin;
- comments and docs: matrices converted on the GPU, checks of the
  parameters of Belos, crash of the distance Laplacian of MueLu on the
  host, hybrid GMRES without outer solver.
